t(25, 2385, """The first state constitution in human history, laid down by the Prophet ﷺ
«In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muhammad the Prophet ﷺ between the believers and Muslims of Quraysh and Yathrib and those who followed them, joined them and strove alongside them: they are one Ummah apart from other people. The Emigrants of Quraysh, according to their custom, pay the blood money among themselves, and they ransom their captives with fairness and justice among the believers. And Banu Awf, according to""")

t(26, 60, """their custom, pay their former blood money, and every group ransoms its captive with fairness and justice among the believers. The same was stated for Banu Sa'idah, Banu Jusham, Banu al-Najjar, Banu Amr ibn Awf, Banu al-Nabit and Banu al-Aws. The believers shall not leave anyone among them burdened with debt without giving to him fairly for ransom or blood money. No believer shall ally with the client of another believer against him. The God-fearing believers are against whoever among them transgresses or seeks to spread injustice, sin, aggression or corruption among the believers; their hands are all against him, even if he is the son of one of them. No believer shall kill a believer for the sake of a disbeliever, nor shall a disbeliever be helped against a believer. The protection of Allah is one: the least of them may grant protection binding on them all. The believers are allies of one another apart from other people. Whoever of the Jews follows us shall have help and equal treatment; they shall not be wronged, nor shall their enemies be aided against them. The peace of the believers is one: no believer shall make peace apart from another believer in fighting in the way of Allah, except on the basis of equality and justice among them. Every raiding party that goes out with us shall take turns, one after another. The believers avenge one another for their blood shed in the way of Allah. The God-fearing believers follow the best and straightest guidance. No polytheist shall give protection to the property or person of Quraysh, nor stand in the way of a believer regarding it. Whoever kills a believer without cause, with clear proof, shall be subject to retaliation for it unless the guardian of the slain is satisfied; all the believers shall be against him, and nothing is lawful for them but to stand against him. It is not lawful for a believer who has affirmed what is in this document and believes in Allah and the Last Day to help a criminal or shelter him; whoever helps or shelters him, upon him is the curse and wrath of Allah on the Day of Resurrection, and no repentance or ransom will be accepted from him. Whatever you differ about, it is to be referred to Allah and to Muhammad. The Jews shall bear expenses along with the believers as long as they are at war. The Jews of Banu Awf are one community
with the believers; the Jews have their religion and the Muslims have theirs; Banu al-Najjar likewise, their clients and themselves, except whoever does wrong or sins, for he destroys only himself and his household. The like of that was stated for the Jews of Banu al-Najjar, Banu al-Harith, Banu Sa'idah, Banu Jusham, Banu al-Aws, Banu Tha'labah and Banu al-Shutbah. Jafnah is a branch of Tha'labah. The close associates of the Jews are as themselves. Righteousness stands before sin. The clients of Tha'labah are as themselves. None of them may go out except with the permission of Muhammad. No one is prevented from avenging a wound. Whoever kills by stealth, it is upon himself, except one who has been wronged. Allah stands with the most faithful observance of this. The Jews bear their expenses and the Muslims bear theirs. Between them is mutual help against whoever fights the people of this document. Between them is sincerity, good counsel and righteousness, not sin. No man is guilty for what his ally does. Help is for the wronged. The interior of Yathrib is a sanctuary for the people of this document. The neighbor is as oneself, neither harmed nor sinning. No woman shall be given protection except with the permission of her family. Whatever incident or dispute arises among the people of this document from which corruption is feared, it is to be referred to Allah and to Muhammad ﷺ. Allah stands with what is most God-fearing and most faithful in this document. No protection shall be given to Quraysh nor to those who help them. Between them is mutual help against whoever attacks Yathrib. If they are called to make a peace and to enter into it, they shall make it and enter into it; and if they call to the like of that, it is their right upon the believers, except for those who fight over religion. Upon every person falls their share from the side that is toward them. The Jews of al-Aws, their clients and themselves, have the same as the people of this document, with pure faithfulness from the people of this document. Righteousness stands before sin. No one earns anything except against himself. Allah stands with what is most truthful and most faithful in this document. This document does not shield a wrongdoer or a sinner. Whoever goes out is safe, and whoever stays in Medina is safe, except one who does wrong or sins. Allah is the protector of whoever is righteous and God-fearing, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ».""")

